// The sturdiness classes of the boxes that carry an HP pool, in HP points per m² of a box's mean
// face. Read by `src/ballistics/box_classes.rs`, embedded and parsed once, validated at parse.
//
// A tank file authors each pool (`hp` in `<tank>.tank.ron`'s `volumes`) as its class × the box's
// measured mean face, the mean of the three axis-aligned face areas of its bounds in the tank's
// sim geometry, rounded to a whole point; `src/tests/box_pools.rs` holds every tank asset to
// within ±25 % of that. The class follows the box's facets: a crew station is `crew`, an
// ammunition box `ammo`, any other box with a pool `hard`. So a box of one class at one place in
// the field fares as any other box of that class there, whatever its size: the field's dose to a
// box grows with the face it presents, and so does its pool. The law is design doc §6,
// `.agents/docs/design/armor-penetration-and-damage.md`; the decision is #3 in
// `.agents/scratch/damage-cam-2026-10-08/research/ap-aphe-2026-10-23/decision-2026-10-23.md`.
//
// PROVENANCE: every value is authored `(value, Kind("source or reason"))`, Kind one of Measured,
// Derived, Tuned, Resolution, Unknown (`src/provenance.rs`); a value without one does not load.
(
    crew: (150, Tuned("owner decision 2026-10-23 (#2, #3): the class the field's calibration in
        spall_cone.ron is set against, a crew box fully inside a weak ordinary perforation's cone
        about 2 m from the hole having its pool emptied. The knockout radius depends on the class
        alone, never the face (DERIVED in spall_cone.ron)")),
    ammo: (150, Tuned("as fragile per m² as a crew station: a propellant case a fragment reaches
        is lost. The hard class would leave a bin a round's line passes straight through in
        action (pen cam scenario s5)")),
    hard: (300, Tuned("owner decision 2026-10-23: sturdier components hold up a little better,
        never through half a cone; twice the crew class per m²")),
)
